/ Stage 4 (ruling 8): the builder offers kinded types by name. Per decision 749 + ruling 1
/ the type's name stays its parent and the sub-sort rides as its kind: `set %n% = "1.5" as
/ decimal` lands %n% as `{number, kind: decimal}`. Today's name assert is green already
/ (baseline: number 5/5), so the kind.name assert is the red one.
AsDecimalKeepsDecimal
- set %n% = "1.5" as decimal
- assert.equals(Expected="number", Actual=%n!type.name%, Message="type.name is number")
- assert.equals(Expected="decimal", Actual=%n!type.kind.name%, Message="type.kind.name is decimal")
